## Intended use

Staff ask questions about approved internal documents and receive short answers with citations
to the passages used. Answers support, and do not replace, the documents and the people who own
them.

## Out of scope

- Decisions about individuals (eligibility, performance, entitlements)
- Legal or financial advice
- Questions about documents above the classification ceiling, which the service never loads
- Acting on anything: the service only answers

## Data

Documents are Markdown files with an id, a title and a classification. Questions are processed
in memory; the audit log keeps a hash of each question, never its text. With the default local
model, no text leaves the machine or server where the service runs.

## How it can fail

- **A wrong answer with a valid citation.** The validator checks that a cited source was given,
  not that the sentence is faithful to it. The monthly sample review looks for exactly this.
- **Not found when the answer exists.** Keyword retrieval misses paraphrases. Add embeddings
  from a local model when the not-found rate shows it.
- **Small local models** follow the citation format less reliably than large ones; withheld
  answers rise. The recorded evaluation shows the rate for each model.

## Evaluation

`evals/cases.jsonl`: answered questions with the expected document, a planted prompt injection,
a document above the ceiling, an out-of-scope question and an empty one. CI runs it with the
deterministic stand-in (plumbing and guardrails) and replays the recorded live run (quality).
Results for each model are in `evals/results/`.

## Human oversight

Answers carry their citations so the reader can check them. Withheld answers are logged with
the reason for review. The owner reviews a sample of real questions each month (OPERATIONS.md).
